 border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133728393.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Melanchton Cliser and his family were among the residents forced from their Virginia home as land was acquired for Shenandoah National Park in the 1930s. Cliser owned 46 acres along US 211 and operated a gas station. In October 1935, the local sheriff and deputies handcuffed him, removed the family's belongings and sealed their house. His case was part of a wider and often contentious effort that displaced hundreds of families from the Blue Ridge Mountains as the park took shape.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1935-melanchthon-cliser-refused-4855-for-his-46-acre-virginia-property-deputies-handcuffed-and-evicted-him-and-he-never-cashed-it-as-shenandoah-national-park-took-shape/articleshow/133728393.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1935-melanchthon-cliser-refused-4855-for-his-46-acre-virginia-property-deputies-handcuffed-and-evicted-him-and-he-never-cashed-it-as-shenandoah-national-park-took-shape/articleshow/133728393.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133730382,imgsize-143543.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Philip Fearnside spent 50 years studying how deforestation, dams and highways reshape the Amazon]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133732280.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[For half a century, Philip Fearnside has delved into the complexities of Amazon development, focusing on the financial and ecological consequences of deforestation and infrastructural advancements. He sheds light on the overlooked costs associated with hydroelectric dams and road construction, asserting that forests provide invaluable benefits beyond mere timber and agricultural outputs. His research brings the often-ignored environmental costs into the public eye, prompting critical discussions among society.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/he-began-studying-the-amazon-in-the-1970s-50-years-later-philip-fearnsides-research-has-calculated-the-costs-of-losing-the-amazon-on-account-of-deforestation-dams-and-highways/articleshow/133732280.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/he-began-studying-the-amazon-in-the-1970s-50-years-later-philip-fearnsides-research-has-calculated-the-costs-of-losing-the-amazon-on-account-of-deforestation-dams-and-highways/articleshow/133732280.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133733019,imgsize-2412668.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[$5M condo shatters Provincetown's real estate record]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133732705.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Provincetown's real estate market has reached new heights, with two condos selling for remarkable prices recently. Notably, a chic three-bedroom home sold for an eye-popping five million dollars, establishing a record for condo sales in the area. As demand skyrockets, buyers are drawn to the allure of contemporary living and resort-like comforts in this sought-after destination, amidst a backdrop of limited housing availability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/provincetowns-most-expensive-condo-sold-for-5m-just-two-weeks-after-another-condo-set-a-3-9m-record-the-unit-found-a-buyer-in-only-five-days/articleshow/133732705.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/provincetowns-most-expensive-condo-sold-for-5m-just-two-weeks-after-another-condo-set-a-3-9m-record-the-unit-found-a-buyer-in-only-five-days/articleshow/133732705.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:50:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133732868,imgsize-466070.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[880s Louisville mansion with 48 rooms lists for $1.95 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133732861.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/built-in-the-1880s-with-48-rooms-a-louisville-mansion-later-helped-inspire-the-speed-art-museum-nearly-140-years-later-it-is-for-sale-for-1-95-million/articleshow/133732861.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/built-in-the-1880s-with-48-rooms-a-louisville-mansion-later-helped-inspire-the-speed-art-museum-nearly-140-years-later-it-is-for-sale-for-1-95-million/articleshow/133732861.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:49:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133732999,imgsize-550758.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Priscilla Chan lost her grandfather in sixth grade; then she found a cancer textbook to learn why]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133732860.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/mark-zuckerbergs-wife-priscilla-chans-grandfather-died-of-cancer-when-she-was-in-sixth-grade-she-found-a-cancer-textbook-and-taught-herself-why-he-died/articleshow/133732860.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/mark-zuckerbergs-wife-priscilla-chans-grandfather-died-of-cancer-when-she-was-in-sixth-grade-she-found-a-cancer-textbook-and-taught-herself-why-he-died/articleshow/133732860.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:57:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133733101,imgsize-721010.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists covered an Amazon plot with 6,000 panels to block rain; biomass fell by a third]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133727852.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Research conducted during an extended drought in Brazil's Caxiuana National Forest indicated initial resilience among trees. However, the eventual failure of large grown trees resulted in major biomass depletion and increased carbon release. As the forest shifted its role from a carbon reservoir to a net carbon emitter, the surviving vegetation adapted to find water, ultimately leading to a structurally distinct forest with diminished carbon storage.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-covered-an-amazon-rainforest-plot-with-6000-panels-to-block-half-its-rain-large-trees-died-and-biomass-fell-by-a-third/articleshow/133727852.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-covered-an-amazon-rainforest-plot-with-6000-panels-to-block-half-its-rain-large-trees-died-and-biomass-fell-by-a-third/articleshow/133727852.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133727963,imgsize-1881940.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Russia to close German cultural centres after Berlin's move over airport attack 'plot']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133731697.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/tit-for-tat-russia-to-close-german-cultural-centres-after-berlins-move-over-airport-attack-plot/articleshow/133731697.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/tit-for-tat-russia-to-close-german-cultural-centres-after-berlins-move-over-airport-attack-plot/articleshow/133731697.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:24:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133732256,imgsize-52364.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Italy's 60-year tradition lets some diners take restaurant plates home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133731991.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/in-italy-some-restaurants-let-diners-take-their-plates-home-the-60-year-tradition-that-turned-plates-into-souvenirs/articleshow/133731991.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/in-italy-some-restaurants-let-diners-take-their-plates-home-the-60-year-tradition-that-turned-plates-into-souvenirs/articleshow/133731991.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:20:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133732157,imgsize-1455020.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A $6.9 billion Ohio data-centre project has sparked a one-year moratorium and ballot fight, here's why]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133729237.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Grove City is facing a split among residents regarding a charter amendment targeting substantial developments, including data centers. Proponents assert this measure safeguards the community's unique character and resources against unchecked growth. In contrast, critics warn that the amendment could stifle potential economic opportunities. The decision on this pivotal amendment will be presented to voters on the November ballot.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-6-9-billion-ohio-data-centre-project-would-cover-about-300-acres-after-resident-backlash-grove-city-imposed-a-one-year-moratorium-and-a-ballot-fight-is-now-underway/articleshow/133729237.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-6-9-billion-ohio-data-centre-project-would-cover-about-300-acres-after-resident-backlash-grove-city-imposed-a-one-year-moratorium-and-a-ballot-fight-is-now-underway/articleshow/133729237.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133729349,imgsize-197928.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Palm Beach’s ‘Ham and cheese house’ bought for $15.975 million in 2013, now listed at $105 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133727685.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Casa Eleda, the historic “Ham And Cheese House” in Palm Beach, Florida, has been listed for $105 million. Built in 1928, the seven-bedroom oceanfront mansion was bought for $15.975 million in 2013. Its owners carried out a multi-year restoration while preserving its historic details. The property has direct ocean access through a private tunnel and includes an oceanfront cabana.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2013-a-couple-paid-15-975-million-for-palm-beachs-1928-ham-and-cheese-house-after-an-award-winning-restoration-the-oceanfront-landmark-is-listed-for-105-million/articleshow/133727685.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2013-a-couple-paid-15-975-million-for-palm-beachs-1928-ham-and-cheese-house-after-an-award-winning-restoration-the-oceanfront-landmark-is-listed-for-105-million/articleshow/133727685.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133728151,imgsize-152368.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Former California mayor sentenced to prison for sexually abusing 17-year-old foreign exchange student]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133731925.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/former-california-mayor-sentenced-to-prison-for-sexually-abusing-17-year-old-foreign-exchange-student/articleshow/133731925.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/former-california-mayor-sentenced-to-prison-for-sexually-abusing-17-year-old-foreign-exchange-student/articleshow/133731925.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:16:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133732116,imgsize-347698.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2001, synthetic estrogen was added to an Ontario lake; its minnow population collapsed after 2 seasons]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133729679.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A groundbreaking experiment conducted in Ontario's Lake 260 unveiled alarming ecological consequences stemming from synthetic estrogen exposure. The minuscule amounts of 17α-ethynylestradiol resulted in reproductive failure among fathead minnows, nearly driving the species to extinction. This critical study highlighted how even minimal contaminant levels can dramatically disrupt aquatic ecosystems. Researchers caution that wastewater containing estrogens poses significant threats to aquatic biodiversity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2001-scientists-began-adding-5-to-6-nanograms-per-litre-of-synthetic-estrogen-to-an-ontario-lake-after-2-seasons-its-minnow-population-collapsed/articleshow/133729679.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2001-scientists-began-adding-5-to-6-nanograms-per-litre-of-synthetic-estrogen-to-an-ontario-lake-after-2-seasons-its-minnow-population-collapsed/articleshow/133729679.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T15:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133729993,imgsize-1633763.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trees planted to stop deserts may be straining water supplies in China]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133679534.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/china-planted-a-huge-forest-belt-to-fight-desertification-scientists-say-the-trees-are-creating-a-carbon-versus-water-trade-off/articleshow/133679534.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/china-planted-a-huge-forest-belt-to-fight-desertification-scientists-say-the-trees-are-creating-a-carbon-versus-water-trade-off/articleshow/133679534.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-02T16:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133680105,imgsize-292956.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Magnitude 5 quake hits Tibet amid ongoing search for hundreds missing after deadly floods]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133731622.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An earthquake of magnitude five struck Tibet on Thursday.  Rescue operations continue following catastrophic flooding near the Gyirong border crossing.  The only road to the crossing reopened, allowing heavy machinery access.  Authorities reported twenty-one deaths and 541 people remain missing.  Landslides continue to pose a significant concern for rescue teams.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/magnitude-5-earthquake-strikes-tibet-days-after-devastating-floods-kill-21-and-leave-hundreds-missing/articleshow/133731622.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/magnitude-5-earthquake-strikes-tibet-days-after-devastating-floods-kill-21-and-leave-hundreds-missing/articleshow/133731622.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T14:54:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133731675,imgsize-602468.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Over 50,000 protest in Madrid over Spain's handling of Cueta migrant crisis]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133730882.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Spain witnessed a large-scale protest as thousands rallied against the recent surge of migrants flooding into Ceuta. Demonstrators demanded the resignation of the Prime Minister and a plan for either repatriation or redistribution of the newcomers. Over seventy thousand migrants breached the Spanish border within just two days in July. The government blames human trafficking and misinformation for the perilous crossings, though Morocco refutes claims of managing this mass movement.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/watch-over-50000-protesters-gather-in-madrid-over-spains-handling-of-cueta-migrant-crisis/articleshow/133730882.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/watch-over-50000-protesters-gather-in-madrid-over-spains-handling-of-cueta-migrant-crisis/articleshow/133730882.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-03T14:23:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133730962,imgsize-72354.cms"/></item></channel></rss>